<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended November 27, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Nov 27  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.05   +0.119    +0.470</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     5.75   -2.180    -3.558</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	464.86   -0.885    +5.183</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 143.50   -0.600   -22.400</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.64   -0.284    +2.059</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			   Oct	   Sept</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-12.92	-12.67</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     658.09	653.27</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    104.57	102.90</p>
<p>					   Oct 96    Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>M1					 65.70	64.23	59.07</p>
<p>M2					393.68     390.76     384.00</p>
<p>M3					492.74     485.18     466.54</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
